    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0401" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1383: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Australia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canberra</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-24T10:00:00+10:00">December 24,
                            1941—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Ministry External Affairs has shown me appeal made yesterday by Prime
                    Minister to President and Churchill<anchor n="83" xml:id="d428-f1"/> and asked
                    me to support it. I do most earnestly support Curtin’s statement of the
                    situation. People in the Pacific area await news of definite movement to stop
                    Japanese advances which if permitted to continue threaten to deprive us of every
                    advantage.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
